WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
而且我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你带来了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们将剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能讲出的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

8
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.940
And welcome to Conflict Resolution.
欢迎收听《冲突调解》。

9
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.660
I'm talking to you from my closet today.
我今天在我的衣帽间里跟你聊天。

10
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.880
I know, we're both in our closets today.
我知道，我们今天都在各自的衣帽间里。

11
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.140
What is happening?
这是怎么回事？

12
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.340
We are both talking to each other from our closets.
我们俩都在衣帽间里跟对方说话。

13
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.120
And Sam and Cody are watching.
萨姆和科迪在看着呢。

14
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.760
I'm looking at Cody's cat.
我在看科迪的猫。

15
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.240
Love it.
太棒了。

16
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.680
Sam's dog is somewhere there.
萨姆的狗就在那里的某个地方。

17
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.020
This is where we're at now, folks.
各位，这就是我们目前的现状。

18
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.220
Angela, your shirts are very well folded.
安吉拉，你的衬衫叠得真整齐。

19
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.400
Are those Josh's shirts?
那些是乔什的衬衫吗？

20
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.260
No, baby girl.
不是的，宝贝女孩。

21
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:51.960
Baby girl.
宝贝女孩。

22
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.600
Are we doing that again this week?
我们这周还要这么叫吗？

23
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:54.880
We are.
我们要的。

24
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:55.800
Here's the thing.
情况是这样的。

25
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.460
I've started every morning by talking to my family in Texas and Louisiana.
我每天早上都是和德克萨斯州和路易斯安那州的家人通话开始的。

26
00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.480
And then it just is kind of with me for the whole day.
然后这种状态就会伴随我一整天。

27
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.500
This is my closet, my own closet.
这是我的衣帽间，我自己的衣帽间。

28
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.620
I share it with no one.
我和任何人都不共享。

29
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.620
It is a personal life victory.
这是我生活中的一次个人小胜。

30
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.700
Oh my gosh, I only get one side of a closet.
哦天哪，我只能用衣帽间的一侧。

31
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.700
We have one closet and I get one side and Lee gets the other.
我们只有一个衣帽间，我用一侧，李用另一侧。

32
00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:24.300
Although, to be honest, I think I have encroached on about a third of his side.
不过说实话，我觉得我已经侵占了他那侧的大约三分之一。

33
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:29.000
Well, Josh has his own closet, but one wall of it is my shoes.
好吧，乔什有他自己的衣帽间，但其中一面墙放的全是我的鞋子。

34
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.740
This is the riveting content that people tuned in for.
这就是人们收听的精彩内容。

35
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.400
I know.
我知道。

36
00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:33.900
I know.
我知道。

37
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.660
Listen, but just bear with me one second.
听着，大家再忍耐我一下。

38
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:43.620
Here is a perk of not growing since like your junior year of high school.
这就是自从高中差不多高二以来就没再长高的好处。

39
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.860
Maybe a little wider in some places, but I've had the same shoe size.
可能某些地方变宽了一点，但我一直都是同一个鞋码。

40
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.020
Angela, you're describing most adults.
安吉拉，你描述的可是绝大多数成年人。

41
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.880
I mean, most adults hit their peak height somewhere around their junior, senior year of high school.
我的意思是，大多数成年人在高中高二或高三左右就达到了身高顶峰。

42
00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.900
It's not like other people are continuing to grow four or five inches in their 20s and 30s.
又不是说别人到了二三十岁还会继续长高四五英寸。

43
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.600
Do you have the same size foot as like when you were a sophomore?
你现在的脚码和上高一高二时一样吗？

44
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:08.130
Yes, of course.
对，当然一样。

45
00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:08.680
You do?
真的吗？

46
00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:12.800
Yeah, I've been a seven and a half medium since like, you know, junior year of high school.
对啊，我从高中差不多高二开始就一直是七号半中码了。

47
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.060
I was fully grown when I went to college.
我上大学的时候就已经完全长成了。

48
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.980
I was fully grown.
我完全长成了。

49
00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.840
Oh, I unzipped my hoodie.
哦，我拉开了连帽衫的拉链。

50
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.480
Could y'all hear that?
大家能听到那个声音吗？

51
00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.620
It sounded like a toot.
听起来像放了个屁。

52
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.300
It sounded like you tooted.
听起来像是你放屁了。

53
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:24.508
What?
什么？

54
00:02:24.508 --> 00:02:25.080
It wasn't a toot.
才不是放屁。

55
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.260
It sounded like a toot.
听起来就像。

56
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:30.400
It's good that you're claiming that you unzipped your hoodie.
你非说那是你在拉开连帽衫拉链，这倒挺好笑的。

57
00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.280
It was.
确实是。

58
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.320
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

59
00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.200
I see how it is.
我算是看清了。

60
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.160
So we're here.
所以我们现在开始了。

61
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.680
It's Conflict Resolution Day, if you can't tell.
如果你们看不出来的话，今天是冲突解决日。

62
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:43.020
It's season two, episode 21, written by Greg Daniels and directed by Charles McDougal.
这是第二季第21集，由格雷格·丹尼尔斯编剧，查尔斯·麦克道格尔执导。

63
00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:43.540
Action!
开拍！

64
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:44.640
Action!
开拍！

65
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.980
This was a really, really fun one for me.
这一集对我和说都真的、真的很开心。

66
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.520
And I love Charles, and he and I got to play a lot in this episode because guess what?
我超喜欢查尔斯，而且在这集里我和他有很多发挥空间，因为你猜怎么着？

67
00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.520
Angela Martin has a lot of conflicts.
安吉拉·马丁有数不清的矛盾。

68
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:55.920
Should I give a summary?
需要我做个总结吗？

69
00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:56.400
Yes.
好呀。

70
00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:56.780
All right.
行吧。

71
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.940
So there are two main things that happen in this episode.
这一集主要发生两件事。

72
00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.640
One, everyone at Dunder Mifflin is being issued an ID badge.
第一，邓德米弗林的每个人都要办工牌。

73
00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.680
So one by one, people go into the break room and have their photo taken for their badge.
大家一个接一个走进休息室，拍照片做工牌。

74
00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:17.880
And then secondly, Michael takes the stack of employee complaints from Toby and starts trying
第二，迈克尔从托比那里拿来了一叠员工投诉，然后开始试图

75
00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.860
to resolve them one by one by forcing people to confront one another at work.
通过强迫大家在工作中当面对质来逐一解决它们。

76
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:23.120
Yeah.
对。

77
00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.680
So I have one little thing about this episode.
所以我对这一集有个小小的想法。

78
00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:31.660
So Dwight is like going on and on about how horrible the security is at the office, right?
就是德鲁伊一直在喋喋不休地说办公室的安保有多烂，对吧？

79
00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:32.500
At Dunder Mifflin.
在邓德米弗林。

80
00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:32.960
Yeah.
对。

81
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.120
We get these badges.
我们领了这些工牌。

82
00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.200
We never wear them again.
然后就再也没戴过。

83
00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:36.660
No.
没错。

84
00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:41.520
Well, you know, there's this deleted scene where it's supposedly the next day and we're
好吧，你知道的，有个被删减的片段里，据说是第二天早晨

85
00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:48.440
all walking in in the morning and we all have our badges on and Hank is in the scene and
我们大家都戴着工牌走进公司，汉克也在那个镜头里，

86
00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:54.420
Hank keeps insisting that Dwight show his ID badge and he pretends like he can't read it
汉克一直坚持要德鲁伊出示工牌，还假装看不清上面写什么，

87
00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.820
and then Dwight misses the elevator.
结果德鲁伊错过了电梯。

88
00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.140
So I guess we wore them once for a tag that never aired.
所以我想我们大概就为了那个从未播出的片尾彩蛋戴过一次吧。

89
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:01.600
Right.
对的。

90
00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.440
But no, we don't ever.
不过说真的，我们再也没戴过。

91
00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.980
It's, you know, it's sort of the casual Friday of it all.
这就有点像那种“周五便服日”的感觉吧。

92
00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:06.380
It is.
确实是。

93
00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:06.560
Right.
对啊。

94
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.500
It really is.
真的是这样。

95
00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:07.720
Yeah.
对。

96
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:08.380
It really is.
真的。

97
00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:08.780
It really.
真的。

98
00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.320
Look, Jen, I brought it back to casual Friday for you.
听着，珍，我为你把“周五便服日”这个梗给接上了。

99
00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:11.960
I appreciate that.
我很感激。

100
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:12.980
I really appreciate that.
我真的很感激。

101
00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.400
Are you going to hit me with some fast facts?
你要用一堆快讯来轰炸我吗？

102
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.120
You know I am.
你知道的，我会的。

103
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.860
I'm going to hit you with some fast facts.
我要用一堆快讯来轰炸你。

104
00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:17.880
Can I get my sting?
能给我放个音效吗？

105
00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:18.940
Fast facts.
快讯。

106
00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:20.220
Yeah.
好啊。

107
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.180
That's from DDB, by the way.
顺便说一句，那是DDB制作的。

108
00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.940
I did not give him a shout out last week.
我上周没有向他致谢。

109
00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.160
So I wanted to do that this week.
所以我这周想这么做。

110
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.260
He's a sound engineer who sent us that sting.
他是一位录音师，给我们发了那个音效。

111
00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.860
Thank you so much for that sting.
非常感谢你提供的音效。

112
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.700
It does make me feel like I'm like in a 1980s game show or something.
这确实让我觉得自己像是在参加上世纪80年代的游戏节目什么的。

113
00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:33.860
Fast facts.
快讯。

114
00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.900
All right.
好吧。

115
00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.200
Fast fact number one.
快讯第一条。

116
00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:42.980
We have a special guest star in this episode playing the ID badge photographer.
我们这集有一位特邀嘉宾客串，饰演工牌摄影师。

117
00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:44.960
It is Scott Adsit.
他就是斯科特·阿德西特。

118
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.360
Scott Adsit.
斯科特·阿德西特。

119
00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.160
I love this fella so much.
我太喜欢这家伙了。

120
00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.760
I've known him a really long time.
我认识他很久了。

121
00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:55.220
He's an improv bud of mine back from the ImprovOlympic days.
他是我的即兴表演搭档，可以追溯到即兴奥林匹克时期。

122
00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.540
And I was texting with him last night.
我昨晚还跟他发短信呢。

123
00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.280
I told him we were watching this episode and he had some fun things to say.
我告诉他我们在看这集，他讲了一些有趣的事情。

124
00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.140
Do you want to hear them?
你想听听吗？

125
00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.020
You know I do.
你知道我想听。

126
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.700
Scott Adsit is an amazing improviser, performer, comedian.
斯科特·阿德西特是一位优秀的即兴表演者、演员、喜剧演员。

127
00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.020
You might know him from 30 Rock.
你可能在《我为喜剧狂》里认识他。

128
00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.480
Also, your children know him as Baymax.
另外，你的孩子们认识他是因为大白。

129
00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.640
He's Baymax and Big Hero 6.
他是《超能陆战队》的大白。

130
00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.700
Anyway, okay.
总之，好吧。

131
00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:17.900
That's my Baymax.
那是我的大白。

132
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.620
Scott, you do it much better.
斯科特，你学得像多了。

133
00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:24.760
So here's a little behind the scenes tidbit that he shared with me that he remembers from filming this episode.
所以这是他跟我分享的一点幕后小花絮，是他对拍摄这一集的记忆。

134
00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:30.460
He said he remembers that Ricky Gervais came to visit set this week and everyone was abuzz.
他说他记得瑞奇·热维斯这周来片场参观了，大家都兴奋不已。

135
00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:42.320
He said that Ricky seemed delighted and surprised by the scale of the production of our set and everything compared to maybe what his production of it had been like in the UK.
他说，与他在英国的制作规模相比，瑞奇似乎对我们片场及各方面的制作规模感到高兴和惊讶。

136
00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.660
And he said that Ricky was just very humble and sweet.
而且他说瑞奇非常谦逊和蔼。

137
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:46.460
Oh my gosh.
哦天哪。

138
00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.740
I did not remember that Ricky visited during this episode.
我不记得瑞奇这集来参观过。

139
00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:53.800
Yeah, I mean, he popped by in and out those first couple seasons, you know.
是啊，我是说，前几季他偶尔会顺道来看看，你知道的。

140
00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.560
But Scott remembered meeting him and he just said that he was just really nice.
但斯科特记得见过他，只说他真的非常好。

141
00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.180
Oh my gosh.
哦天哪。

142
00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:02.060
That's like a fast fact within a fast fact.
这就像是快讯里的快讯。

143
00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:02.720
What?
什么？

144
00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.320
That's a double fast fact.
这是双倍快讯。

145
00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.080
Did I help you get a double fast fact?
我帮你要到了双倍快讯吗？

146
00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:06.700
You did.
是的。

147
00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:07.340
You did.
是的。

148
00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:11.400
Angela, I have a fun fact within this fast fact.
安吉拉，这个快讯里还有一个趣事。

149
00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.520
Both you and Scott have appeared in two episodes of the TV show Monk.
你和斯科特都出演过电视剧《神探阿蒙》的两集。

150
00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.560
I was in one episode, yes, and I played the murderer.
我演过一集，是的，我演的是凶手。

151
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.820
Well, Scott was on seasons three and four.
嗯，斯科特演了第三季和第四季。

152
00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.880
So between the two of you, you cover four seasons of Monk.
所以你们两个加起来，正好覆盖了《神探阿蒙》的四季。

153
00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:28.800
Congratulations.
恭喜啊。

154
00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:30.440
That's my fun fact.
这就是我的趣味冷知识。

155
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:35.480
Monk was so much fun to shoot and Tony Shalhoub was the niceSt.
拍《神探阿蒙》真的特别开心，托尼·夏尔赫布人超级好。

156
00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:42.620
We sat on like a little bench in between scenes and he was throwing something to try to get it in the trash can.
我们俩在两场戏的间隙坐在一张小长椅上，他拿着什么东西往垃圾桶里扔，想把它投进去。

157
00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.440
And when it hit the trash can, it made like a ping-wong.
当它砸中垃圾桶时，发出了类似“叮咚”的声音。

158
00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.020
And I started laughing and he started laughing.
然后我笑了，他也笑了。

159
00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:50.960
And I said, I mean, that was kind of a funny noise.
我说，我是说，那个声音挺搞笑的。

160
00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:57.560
And then the two of us sat there and did our impressions of the noises of things going in the trash can.
接着我们两个就坐在那儿，模仿各种东西掉进垃圾桶时的声音。

161
00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:07.640
Like, I don't know.
就，我不知道。

162
00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.420
He's just so fun.
他这个人太有趣了。

163
00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.380
I just adored him.
我简直太喜欢他了。

164
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.560
That fast fact was just chock full of fun and fast facts.
刚才那个冷知识简直塞满了各种好玩又快速的知识点。

165
00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.460
That was a very full fast fact.
那真是一个内容扎实的快节奏知识点。

166
00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.160
It was a full fast fact.
确实是个内容扎实的快节奏知识点。

167
00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.900
It was a full, fun, double fast fact.
这是一个内容扎实、妙趣横生的双倍快节奏知识点。

168
00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.740
Fantastically fun, full fast fact.
妙趣横生、内容扎实的快节奏知识点。

169
00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.360
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

170
00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:27.920
Fast fact number two.
快节奏知识点之二。

171
00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.020
Okay.
好啦。

172
00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:32.280
Fast fact number two is a fan question from Zach Akers.
快节奏知识点之二是来自扎克·阿克斯的粉丝提问。

173
00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.100
And here's what he wrote in to say.
他是这样写信来问的。

174
00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:48.740
Why does Jim do his talking heads in front of the outside facing window while everyone else's talking heads are inside of the window that faces the bullpen of the office?
为什么吉姆的单采镜头总是在朝向外面的窗户前拍摄，而其他所有人的单采镜头都在朝向办公室开阔区的窗户里面拍摄？

175
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:56.260
He says, in Booze Cruise and some later episodes, there are joint Jim-Pam talking heads in front of the outside window.
他说，在《酒水游轮》以及后面的一些剧集里，有吉姆和帕姆一起面对外窗的联合单采。

176
00:07:56.420 --> 00:08:01.360
But neither Pam nor anyone else normally sits in front of that outside window.
但通常帕姆或其他任何人都不会坐在那个外窗前面。

177
00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:09.140
And then he noticed, because Jim has several talking heads in this one, he was like, it's really prominent in this episode that Jim is there.
然后他注意到，由于吉姆在这集里有很多单采镜头，他就想，吉姆坐在那儿在这集里实在太显眼了。

178
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:16.760
So I thought that was a great question and such a wise observation I had to investigate.
所以我认为这是个很棒的问题，而且观察力如此敏锐，我不得不去调查一下。

179
00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.500
No, that is a great catch.
不，这真的抓得太准了。

180
00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:20.560
It really is.
确实如此。

181
00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:25.940
So I emailed Greg Daniels and I asked him, was this deliberate?
所以我给格雷格·丹尼尔斯发了封邮件，问他，这是刻意安排的吗？

182
00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.260
Was this an accident?
这纯属巧合吗？

183
00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.240
What does he have to say?
他怎么说？

184
00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:36.620
And he said that it was something that Randall Einhorn, our cinematographer, suggested to Greg, starting with the pilot.
他说这是我们的摄影指导兰德尔·艾恩霍恩从试播集开始就向格雷格建议的一个想法。

185
00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.800
And Greg absolutely loved it.
而且格雷格非常喜欢。

186
00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:46.200
He said Randall's intention here was that it didn't necessarily have to be only Jim.
他说兰德尔的本意是，这不一定非得局限于吉姆。

187
00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:59.600
But the idea was that any character that had a future outside of Dunder Mifflin or held some sort of internal optimism would sit in front of a window leading out into the world.
但这个想法是，任何在邓德米夫林之外有未来，或者怀有某种内在乐观精神的角色，都会坐在通往外面世界的窗户前。

188
00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:11.360
But characters who didn't want to leave Dunder Mifflin or who maybe were in more of a position of being trapped would do their talking heads facing into the office.
而那些不想离开邓德米夫林，或者可能处于更有被困感之中的角色，他们的单采镜头则会面向办公室内部。

189
00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:12.000
Wow.
哇。

190
00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:13.180
That's so deep.
这太有深度了。

191
00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.240
That's really deep.
真的很深奥。

192
00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:23.560
Yeah, I'm sitting here racking my brain to think of my character ever sat on that other wall with the window facing out behind her.
是啊，我在这里绞尽脑汁地想，我的角色是不是也曾坐在另一面墙前，背后就是朝外的窗户。

193
00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:29.780
And the one that comes to my mind, and I think it might be the only one I'm trying to think if there's any other one.
我能想到的，而且我觉得可能也是唯一的一个——我在想还有没有别的。

194
00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:33.480
It was when you and I did Big Pregs, Little Pregs.
就是你和我做《大孕妇，小孕妇》那一期的时候。

195
00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:34.700
Yeah, we did.
对，我们做过。

196
00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:38.040
I think it's the only time I ever sat there.
我觉得那是唯一一次我坐在那儿。

197
00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:49.260
Well, for a very long time, I only sat there if I was with Jim, which was really the only possible future for Pam outside of the office.
好吧，很长一段时间里，我只有在和吉姆在一起时才会坐在那儿，这其实也是帕姆在办公室外唯一可能的未来。

198
00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:50.780
Wow.
哇。

199
00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:51.700
I think.
我觉得是这样。

200
00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:52.300
That's so deep.
这太有深度了。

201
00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.440
Isn't that crazy?
这不是太疯狂了吗？

202
00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:59.120
But otherwise, she was rather trapped in her, you know, bad decision of being with Roy.
但从另一方面讲，她被困在了她自己那个，你知道的，和罗伊在一起的错误决定里。

203
00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.140
Trapped or content, you know?
是被困住还是挺满足的，你知道吗？

204
00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.420
I mean, some of us were just happy with our lot in life.
我是说，我们当中有些人对自己的生活现状挺满意的。

205
00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:04.900
Yes.
是的。

206
00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:08.640
Um, well, that is fascinating, and I like it.
嗯，好吧，这太有意思了，我很喜欢。

207
00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.500
Yeah, I thought that was a good one.
对，我觉得这个观点很好。

208
00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:14.380
So thank you so much, Zach, for pointing that out and writing in.
所以非常感谢扎克指出来并写信告诉我们。

209
00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:20.300
Now, finally, fast fact number three, Angela, it's a fast fact flashback.
那么最后，冷知识第三条，安杰拉，这是一个冷知识闪回。

210
00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:21.360
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

211
00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.120
What's up?
怎么啦？

212
00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:22.840
Are you drunk?
你喝醉了吗？

213
00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.040
So here is this fast fact.
所以冷知识是这样的。

214
00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:29.380
This episode was filmed during May 2006.
这一集是在2006年5月拍摄的。

215
00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:34.820
And so, Angela, my question for both of us is, what were you doing?
所以，安杰拉，我给咱俩出的问题是，你当时在干什么？

216
00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.380
Flashback now to May 2006, and what were you up to?
现在闪回到2006年5月，你都在忙些什么？

217
00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:45.720
Well, I had a journal entry from May 3rd, 2006.
嗯，我有一篇2006年5月3日的日记。

218
00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.000
This is what I wrote.
我是这么写的。

219
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:55.500
I wrote that I was doing a photo shoot with my cat, Lucy, for Cat Fancy Magazine.
我写道，我正和我的猫露西一起为《爱猫》杂志拍摄一组照片。

220
00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:56.700
Angela Kinsey.
安杰拉·金西。

221
00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:57.080
What?
什么？

222
00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.480
Shut the front door right now.
简直不敢相信。

223
00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:58.920
What?
什么？

224
00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.180
Do you know what I wrote in my journal?
你知道我在日记里写了什么吗？

225
00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:00.520
No.
不知道。

226
00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.740
For this week of May.
在五月的这一周里。

227
00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.080
What?
什么？

228
00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:02.960
Of 2006.
2006年的。

229
00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:09.600
I did a photo shoot with my cat, Andy, for People Magazine.
我和我的猫安迪一起为《人物》杂志拍了一组照片。

230
00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:10.920
I'm not joking, lady.
我没开玩笑，女士。

231
00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:17.200
Lady, lady, how did we not know that we did photo shoots with our cats at this time?
天哪，天哪，为什么我们当时不知道我们都跟自己的猫拍过写真？

232
00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:25.290
I feel like we probably at the time knew, but it's hilarious to me for us to both share
我觉得我们当时可能知道，但现在我们俩分享2006年5月初的日记，

233
00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:31.290
our journal entries from early May 2006, and we were both so tickled that we were taking
我还是觉得太搞笑了，我们俩当时都对跟猫咪拍照

234
00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.670
photos with our cats.
感到那么津津乐道。

235
00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.290
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

236
00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:36.970
First of all, this is why we're BFFs, all right?
首先，这就是为什么我们是死党，好吗？

237
00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:37.890
This is why.
这就是原因。

238
00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.830
Our life has very strange ways that it is parallel.
我们的人生以非常神奇的方式平行着。

239
00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.870
So, was Lucy on the cover of Cat Fancy?
那么，露西上了《爱猫》的封面吗？

240
00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:48.330
No, Lucy was not on the cover because she was a rescue.
没有，露西没上封面，因为她是一只收养的猫。

241
00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.370
She was not a purebred cat.
她不是纯种猫。

242
00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:54.450
But also, Jenna, Cat Fancy doesn't let humans on the cover.
而且，珍娜，《爱猫》杂志不让人类上封面。

243
00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.230
So, that's like, it's only cats on the cover.
所以，封面上只有猫。

244
00:11:58.370 --> 00:11:58.630
Okay.
好吧。

245
00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:03.170
But the cool thing was is that Lucy and I got like, I think, I mean, I saved the magazine.
但酷炫的是，我和露西得到了，我想，我的意思是，我把杂志存着呢。

246
00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:04.810
I think we got like four pages.
我觉得我们占了大概四页。

247
00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:08.870
So, Lucy and I are in the center, I guess, for the centerfold.
所以我和露西在中间，我猜，就在中间插页上。

248
00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.710
Oh, you are the centerfold of Cat Fancy magazine.
哦，你是《爱猫》杂志的中心插页女郎。

249
00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:14.530
So, Lucy and I look amazing.
所以我和露西看起来棒极了。

250
00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.810
They're some of the best pictures I feel like I have.
我觉得这是我拥有的最棒的一些照片。

251
00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.450
How was she during the photo shoot?
她拍照的时候表现怎么样？

252
00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:20.690
Well, yeah, I should probably give you some backstory about Lucy.
嗯，对，我可能得先给你讲讲露西的背景故事。

253
00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:21.770
Lucy loved to sleep.
露西最喜欢睡觉。

254
00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:22.050
Oh.
哦。

255
00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.130
So, Lucy did nothing.
所以，露西什么都不做。

256
00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:25.670
Lucy just laid there.
露西就躺在那儿。

257
00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:29.670
And I mean, Lucy, I love her.
我是说，露西，我很爱她。

258
00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:30.610
R.I.P.
安息吧。

259
00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:30.930
Lucy.
露西。

260
00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:32.090
She had a great long life.
她度过了漫长而美好的一生。

261
00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:34.930
But she really just loved to lounge.
但她其实就是喜欢躺着。

262
00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.190
She was a lounger.
她是个标准的躺神。

263
00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:36.510
Oh.
哦。

264
00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:41.570
So, I, in many shots, I'm just laying next to her because that's like her favorite thing to do.
所以，在很多镜头里，我都只是躺在她旁边，因为那是她最喜欢做的事。

265
00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:43.830
But what about you?
那你呢？

266
00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:46.150
What was your People magazine shoot like with Andy?
你和安迪一起拍《人物》杂志是什么样子的？

267
00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:51.690
Okay, well, Andy was also a rescue, but he was a semi-feral cat.
好吧，安迪也是一只救助猫，但他是一只半野猫。

268
00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:53.890
I had found him.
是我找到他的。

269
00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:58.970
He was eating out of a dumpster back in Kirksville, Missouri, where I went to college.
他当时在我上大学的密苏里州柯克斯维尔市的一个垃圾桶里找吃的。

270
00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:02.710
I think he was about like five or six months old when I got him.
我带他回家时，他大概五六个月大吧。

271
00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:06.790
And he was just always a little, we said he was always a little wild.
而且他一直都有点，我们说他一直都有点野。

272
00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:10.710
And he loved me and he snuggled me and he was so gentle and sweet.
他很爱我，喜欢依偎着我，而且非常温柔可亲。

273
00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:13.530
But he didn't love strangers in the house.
但他不喜欢家里来陌生人。

274
00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:20.590
And so, when the People magazine guys came over, not only were they all there kind of
所以，当《人物》杂志的人来的时候，他们不仅在那儿

275
00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:25.050
causing a ruckus, you know, and Andy was a little bit like, I'm out of here.
大惊小怪的，你知道的，而且安迪当时有点想说：我可要溜了。

276
00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:29.990
They wanted to do the photo shoot outside and they wanted me to hold him.
他们想在外面拍写真，还想让我抱着他。

277
00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:30.710
Forget it.
想都别想。

278
00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:31.750
Mine was inside.
我的是在室内拍的。

279
00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:32.150
Oh.
哦。

280
00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:32.990
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

281
00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:38.910
Angela, I'm in like full hair and makeup with this dress on.
安吉拉，我当时顶着全套发型和妆容，穿着这身裙子。

282
00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.870
They were like, okay, we're ready for you.
他们说，好吧，我们准备好了。

283
00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:42.030
Will you come out with Andy?
你能带安迪出来吗？

284
00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:48.290
So, I'm holding Andy and I think if you look in the photo, you can see that he and I are
所以，我抱着安迪，我想如果你看那张照片，你会发现我和他

285
00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:54.190
both a little tense, but I'm smiling super big as if I'm not tense.
都有点紧绷，但我笑得超级灿烂，就好像我一点也不紧张一样。

286
00:13:54.490 --> 00:14:00.290
And I wrote in my journal, Angela, I wrote in my journal that he clawed my stomach and
我在日记里写了，安吉拉，我在日记里写了，他把我的肚子抓伤了

287
00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:05.910
I had like, like bloody claw marks in my stomach from the photo shoot because he wanted to get
拍照的时候我肚子上留下了像血爪印一样的抓痕，因为他想逃跑

288
00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:06.250
away.
离开。

289
00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:08.610
Aw, lady.
天哪，姑娘。

290
00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:15.950
I can't believe that we both did cat photo shoots in May of 2006 and also that we both
真不敢相信我们俩都在2006年5月拍过猫咪写真，而且我们俩都

291
00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:20.410
wrote about it in our journals and also that our experiences were so vastly different.
在日记里写了这件事，而且我们的经历竟然如此大相径庭。

292
00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:26.390
I do remember like calling my mom and I was so excited because I hadn't really been in
我还记得当时给我妈打电话，我超级兴奋，因为我这辈子

293
00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:29.110
any magazines ever, obviously, in my whole life.
显然从来没上过什么杂志。

294
00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:32.290
And I was like, mom, I'm going to be in cat fancy.
我就对她说：妈，我要上《Cat Fancy》杂志了。

295
00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.590
And my mom was like, what?
我妈说：什么？

296
00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:40.630
Anyway, that is so cute.
总之，太可爱了。

297
00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:41.210
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

298
00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:44.630
Now I really want to see, I remember you doing that, but now I need to see the picture.
现在我真的很想看看，我记得你拍过这个，但我现在得看看那张照片。

299
00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:44.910
Okay.
好吧。

300
